---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Delete account — Trypup" description="How to delete your Trypup account and all associated data." lang="en" alt="/smazat-ucet/">
  <section class="section wrap prose">
    <h1>Delete account and data</h1>
    <p class="meta">Controller: OndysLab s.r.o. · <a href="mailto:support@trypup.life">support@trypup.life</a></p>

    <p>Trypup works without an account. If you created one, you can delete it and all associated data at any time.</p>

    <h2>1) In the app (fastest)</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open the Trypup app.</li>
      <li>In <strong>Profile</strong>, tap the card with your email; the <strong>Account</strong> screen opens.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>"Delete account"</strong> and confirm.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>This permanently removes your account (email, identifier) and the cloud backup of your saved progress and of your dogs from Dog at home mode.</p>

    <h2>2) By email (if you no longer have the app)</h2>
    <p>Email us from the address you registered with at <a href="mailto:support@trypup.life?subject=Account%20deletion%20request">support@trypup.life</a> with the subject "Account deletion request". We will delete your account and data within 30 days and confirm the deletion.</p>

    <h2>What data is deleted</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Email address and account identifier (authentication).</li>
      <li>Cloud backup of saved progress (dog, training, daily progress, purchased features).</li>
      <li>Cloud backup of dogs from Dog at home mode (dog details, health diary, care plan and reminders, contacts).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Data stored only locally on your device is removed by uninstalling the app. Deleting your account does not remove your dogs' Dog at home details from your phone; you can delete them in the app in <strong>Settings → Dog data</strong>, or one dog at a time on the dog's page → Delete dog. See our <a href="/en/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for more.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
